{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
  "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Paul W. Cane, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our basic principal of evidence of the need for foundation explains why the court of appeals should be reversed. An employment decision is made by the person who made it, the decision-maker. If some other person harbors bias, that's unfortunate; but it is not probative of claims by a plaintiff who is not affected by it. This Court's discrimination cases, both in the employment context and in other contexts, consistently focus on the decision maker's intent, not on the intent of other persons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you were to read the district court's minute order -- and this is that short minute order -- as saying that evidence of pattern and practice simply is not admissible, that would be error, would it not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul W. Cane, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yeah, if the district court had held that under no circumstances could a pattern or practice of discrimination be shown, I think that would have been error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you mean by that? You repeated several times there must be -- must lay a foundation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul W. Cane, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think, in a company that was not small, where a nexus could be inferred, that there was consultation or that there were directions from more senior management, then I think that would be an appropriate foundation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You agree that it has to be a case-by-case determination? There's no absolute rule either way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If that's the way to do it, you didn't do it that way, did you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul W. Cane, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is correct. Had the \"me, too\" evidence been admitted, then we would have had to respond with what might be called \"not you, either\" evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I see your -- does 404 bear on the case, Rule 404 of the Rules of Evidence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Evidence of discrimination by other supervisors within the company is sometimes but not always admissible in a disparate-treatment case to help prove discrimination by the plaintiff's own supervisor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, but here you have a company of 70,000 people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: The determination of the relevance of the \"me, too\" evidence -- and I assume also the 403 status -- needs to be made at the motion in limine stage, or is it a question for the jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Garre",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Furnco case, the Court said that -- that the evidence doesn't have to conclusively demonstrate the fact. It simply has to be relevant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If we find that it would not have been abuse of discretion, then how could we affirm the Tenth Circuit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Egan",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Barred evidence of culture. We had evidence of culture from open remarks, that someone needs to be \"blessed with lots of runway ahead of them\" in order to get a good rating."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I went through to kind of pin down what the facts of consequence were. I went through the offer of proof. I don't have my notes in front of me, but I think my recollection is right on this. It struck me that the admissible evidence that was indicated by the offer of proof boils down basically to this: There were three employees who would testify that, following their dismissal, some or all of their work was done by a younger person."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Has this Court said that 403 determinations must always be made on the record?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It seems very strange to me that we -- there's been -- the case went to the jury without the evidence you wanted to get in. The jury found for the company. Now if the -- if the trial court is going to properly exclude the evidence under 403, we should then have the very same trial with a new jury? That doesn't seem proper."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Egan",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The only thing that can't happen on remand -- I want to make sure this is clear -- is that the judge can't exclude on the same basis that caused the problem the first time; that is, well, it is not Reddick; it's excluded. Not Reddick, it's excluded. Any other factors would be open."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the -- how can we make that assumption when the Tenth Circuit says we know why this district judge ruled as he or she did? We had a precedent. It -- it dealt with employee discipline. We said, categorically, it's got to be the same supervisor; otherwise it's not relevant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cane",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Neither that case nor this case involved any attempt to show that foundation, the linkage between these other persons, these other alleged bad actors, and the decision here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cane",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "should have applied the presumption that an evidentiary ruling is correct rather than incorrect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did anyone argue that before December 15, 2004, that we don't know about the mine run of cases, but this case, in fact it's a waste of time? Did anyone argue that before December 15, 2004?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you not think that there is an important value that the Tenth Circuit recognized in making it clear that there is no absolute bar? If we just assume in favor of the district court, when we don't know that the district court didn't take it as an absolute rule, that -- this is a point of law that should be clarified for the benefit of district courts. Either there's a categorical bar or there's not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cane",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that, absent some showing of relationship of nexus, then the presumptive rule in the run of cases should be that this evidence should not be admitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Solicitor General in his brief said three things with which we agree: the plaintiff's burden to lay foundation; anecdotes don't comprise --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1221",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b0ab5dc9f7c36551022754c7ca9a475edab2b909b6e3835cb0403f2da87bf47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b0ab5dc9f7c-0003-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
